Add a setting to skip the opening movies

`skip_opening_movies=1` in the [system] section of fallout.cfg goes straight to
the main menu instead of playing the publisher logo and the intro first.
Fallout 2 CE has the same setting. In a browser the game is started far more
often than a desktop install, which makes the two unskippable-by-default
movies wear thin quickly.
---
diff --git a/src/game/main.cc b/src/game/main.cc
index 4f8efc1..211380d 100644
--- a/src/game/main.cc
+++ b/src/game/main.cc
@@ -96,8 +96,14 @@ int gnw_main(int argc, char** argv)
         return 1;
     }
 
-    gmovie_play(MOVIE_IPLOGO, GAME_MOVIE_FADE_IN);
-    gmovie_play(MOVIE_INTRO, 0);
+    // CE: Allow to skip the opening movies (same setting as Fallout 2 CE).
+    int skipOpeningMovies = 0;
+    config_get_value(&game_config, GAME_CONFIG_SYSTEM_KEY, "skip_opening_movies", &skipOpeningMovies);
+
+    if (skipOpeningMovies == 0) {
+        gmovie_play(MOVIE_IPLOGO, GAME_MOVIE_FADE_IN);
+        gmovie_play(MOVIE_INTRO, 0);
+    }
 
     if (main_menu_create() == 0) {
         int language_filter = 1;
